WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.150
These aren't nests.

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:04.280
They're waste dumps for
a truly monster tunneling

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.610
project, a termite
megacity the size of

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.570
Great Britain.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:14.380
It dwarfs any city that
humans have ever built.

00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:16.060
It's mind boggling.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.130
Analysis suggests that
every year the insects

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.460
here excavate over 50
million tons of soil.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.460
The amount that's been
moved around to build

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.000
these tremendous mounds
is the equivalent of 4000

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.860
great Pyramids of Giza.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:36.770
This is a huge structure
built by tiny insects.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.540
Soil analysis confirms
some of these insect

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:43.920
mounds are 4000 years
old, built more than 2000

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.560
years before the rise of
the Roman Empire.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.990
And the excavation that
produced them is the most

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.080
extensive bioengineering
effort by a single insect

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.520
species anywhere on the
planet.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.170
This is actually a mega
city.

